This is the classic Word Ladder problem. I need to find the shortest transformation sequence length using BFS.

Approach:
1. If endWord is not in wordList, return 0.
2. Build a set of words for O(1) lookup.
3. BFS from beginWord, at each step try all possible single-letter transformations (26 letters per position), check if the transformed word is in the set.
4. Count levels; when we reach endWord, return the level count.

Alternative optimization: use the "wildcard" pattern approach - for each word, generate patterns like "*it", "h*t", "hi*" and build an adjacency map. This is more efficient for long word lists.

Let me write the standard BFS with pattern-based adjacency:

```javascript
var ladderLength = function(beginWord, endWord, wordList) {
    if (!wordList.includes(endWord)) return 0;

    const L = beginWord.length;
    const allCombo = new Map();

    for (const word of wordList) {
        for (let i = 0; i < L; i++) {
            const pattern = word.slice(0, i) + '*' + word.slice(i + 1);
            if (!allCombo.has(pattern)) allCombo.set(pattern, []);
            allCombo.get(pattern).push(word);
        }
    }

    const queue = [[beginWord, 1]];
    const visited = new Set([beginWord]);

    while (queue.length > 0) {
        const [word, level] = queue.shift();
        for (let i = 0; i < L; i++) {
            const pattern = word.slice(0, i) + '*' + word.slice(i + 1);
            const neighbors = allCombo.get(pattern) || [];
            for (const next of neighbors) {
                if (next === endWord) return level + 1;
                if (!visited.has(next)) {
                    visited.add(next);
                    queue.push([next, level + 1]);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return 0;
};
```

